      "text": "There are two companies that don’t care about market crashes. \n\n$APP down 19.7%\n$DNKG down 19.4%\n$PINS down to 19.1%\n$ASTS down 15.21%\n$RDW down to 13.1% \n$USAR down 12.4%\nSilver down 11.6%\n$OSS down 9.58%\n$RGTI down 8.85%\n$RDDT down 6.8%\n$RKLB down 5.4%\n$APPL down 5.09%\nGold down 3.4%\nSPY Index down 1.54%\n\nSandisk up 7.21%. \n\nThe other biggest gainer? Walmart, up 3.78% today.\n\nYou have a fwd 2027 p/e ~7 memory company growing net income at triple digits y/y.\n\nAnd a bath towel reseller growing in line with inflation sitting at 46 p/e, outperforming the market.\n\nMarkets are starting to make less and less sense.",
